<title>GERMANY: Lehman Bros upgrade boosts VW stock.</title>
<headline>Lehman Bros upgrade boosts VW stock.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German carmaker Volkswagen AG rose against the trend in bourse dealings Friday after Lehman Brothers said it had upgraded the stock to &quot;outperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot;.</p>
<p>The stock, which had already been firm while the broader market fell, rose as much as four marks to 604 marks after the recommendation was released before settling at 602.50 marks, up 2.50 marks at 1115 GMT.</p>
<p>The 30-share DAX index was down 1.5 percent at 2,804.61 points.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
